{"etape": 9, "horodatage_utc": "2026-10-21T11:52:37.096253Z", "outil": "send_message_to_user", "arguments": {"message": "I've priced out the options. Here are the details:\n\n**Cheapest business round trip (same dates), per passenger:**\n- **Outbound – Sun 2024-05-26:** HAT023 JFK → SFO, 14:00–20:00, direct — **$364**\n- **Return – Tue 2024-05-28:** HAT204 SFO → SEA 08:00–10:00 ($248) + HAT100 SEA → JFK 13:00–19:00 ($259) — **$507**\n- **Total per passenger: $871 → × 3 passengers = $2,613**\n\n**Option A — Cancel + rebook (your preference):**\n- Cancellation: your reservation was created 2024-05-14 16:03 (within 24 hrs) and no flight has been flown, so it is eligible. Refund of **$567** goes back to the original payment method (gift card ...6136092) within 5–7 business days, so it will **not** be available for today's purchase.\n- New booking payment (in this order):\n  - Certificate ...3765853: **$500** (only one certificate can be used per reservation)\n  - Gift card ...8020792: **$198**\n  - Gift card ...6136092: **$129** (current balance)\n  - **Mastercard ...2198526: $1,786**\n\n**Option B — Just change cabin to business on existing flights:**\n- New fare total $1,065 × 3 = $3,195, minus the $567 already paid = **$2,628 due**, and flight changes must be paid with a single gift card or credit card (certificates not allowed) → **Mastercard charge $2,628**\n\nSo **Option A is cheaper for your Mastercard ($1,786 vs $2,628)**, as you expected.\n\nTo proceed with Option A, please confirm:\n1. Cancellation reason — is it **change of plan**?\n2. You approve cancelling K1NW8N and booking the new business round trip above with the payment breakdown shown (Mastercard charged $1,786)?"}, "resultat": "Yes, I approve proceeding with Option A. The cancellation reason is \"change of plan.\"\n\nHowever, I have a great idea to use all three certificates. Since only one certificate can be used per reservation, I'd like to book three separate reservations.\n\nFor myself, I will use the $500 certificate and all gift cards.\nFor Aarav, I will use certificate_9984806.\nFor Evelyn, I will use the other certificate.\n\nI will pay the rest with my Mastercard. At the end of the day, I want to know the total amount my Mastercard will be charged across all three reservations.", "erreur": null}
{"etape": 10, "horodatage_utc": "2026-10-21T11:52:45.646755Z", "outil": "send_message_to_user", "arguments": {"message": "That works within our rules — each reservation can hold one certificate, and a reservation can have as few as one passenger. Here's the plan and the Mastercard total:\n\n**All three reservations:** round trip, business class, same flights — HAT023 JFK→SFO 2024-05-26, then HAT204 SFO→SEA + HAT100 SEA→JFK 2024-05-28. No bags, no insurance.\n\n| Reservation | Passenger | Fare | Certificate | Gift cards | Mastercard |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Mohamed Silva | $871 | ...3765853 ($500) | ...8020792 ($198) + ...6136092 ($129) | **$44** |\n| 2 | Aarav | $871 | ...9984806 ($250) | — | **$621** |\n| 3 | Evelyn | $871 | ...2765295 ($250) | — | **$621** |\n\n**Total Mastercard charge across all three reservations: $1,286**\n\n(Note: the $567 cancellation refund still goes to gift card ...6136092 within 5–7 business days, so it can't be applied today.)\n\nTo proceed I need the following, and then I'll cancel K1NW8N and book the three reservations:\n1. **Aarav's last name and date of birth**\n2. **Evelyn's last name and date of birth**\n\nAlso, please confirm the passenger names already on file for you are correct: **Mohamed Silva, DOB 1960-11-26**."}, "resultat": "Thank you for breaking that down. The total Mastercard charge of $1,286 is much better!\n\nMy last name is Silva, so Aarav's last name is Silva, and his date of birth is 2015-03-10.\nEvelyn's last name is also Silva, and her date of birth is 2018-07-22.\n\nAnd yes, my name and date of birth are correct: Mohamed Silva, DOB 1960-11-26.", "erreur": null}
